// Fund payment duty, information duties, suspension liberties and sanctions:
// L. 511-1 (fund duty to pay), L. 552-2 (payment conditional on health
// certificates - liberty to suspend), L. 552-6 (delegue costs on the
// serving body), L. 554-2 (paid intermediaries: prohibition + 4 500 EUR
// fine), L. 554-3 (court liberty to order judgment insertion, 150 EUR
// cost ceiling), L. 583-1 (information/assistance duties), L. 583-3
// (suspension liberty on refused checks).
//
// RESTORED 2026-10-08 (FINISH payment-core, no-run authoring). The module
// expected by package.law, the duty-bearer inventory and the six
// registered devoir-paiement suites was absent from the tree; the norms
// below follow the inventory names and the suite expectations exactly.
// L. 511-1 / L. 583-1 / L. 583-3 sit outside the payment-core article
// group but inside this package: they are restored here as source/test
// diagnostic repair (COMPARE finish-coord request 2026-10-08), anchored
// on this package's pinned fragments, no model invention.
//
// DEONTIC MAP:
// - L. 511-1 (catalogue scope) + R. 553-1 (monthly settlement at term
//   due) - fund duty to settle the catalogue benefits due from their
//   R. 552-2 date (duty, maintain prestation_versee); premises -
//   allocataire + debtor fund + prestations_dues_a_compter (PC-R07-07:
//   the L. 511-1 enumeration alone states no payment duty).
// - L. 552-2 "peut etre subordonne" - fund liberty to suspend the AF/CF
//   fraction of a child below compulsory-school age absent health
//   certificates (explicit stated age premise; the school-age threshold
//   itself is education-code external); suspension duration and
//   modalities - decree L. 584-1, boundary (unpinned).
// - L. 552-6 metropole + L. 755-4 DOM (PC-R03-09 split, PC-R04-05
//   benefit-specific): judge liberty to order the delegate measure +
//   delegue costs (duty, single/several rules each). Metropole L. 552-6
//   has no prime exclusion; DOM L. 755-4 excludes the prime forfaitaire
//   (L. 524-5 II, al. 2) at benefit level: single-eligible duty needs
//   the eligible serving body + no prime, multi duty needs the highest
//   eligible payer among remaining benefits (prime may coexist).
//   Territory is caller-stated (beneficiaire_dom_l7554; six L. 751-1
//   collectivities; metropole = the explicit negative, SPEC 69 - absence
//   states neither, D-42 12.10.2026). Highest(-eligible) body is
//   caller-side maximum (boundary B-PFCORE-DELEGUE-MAX).
// - L. 554-2 "sera puni" - prohibitions on paid benefit-procurement
//   services, direct offer and caused offer ("fait offrir": separate
//   prohibition FaireOffrirServicesRemuneres, holder: the intermediary,
//   E1330 pattern) + 4 500 EUR fine built by rule AmendeIntermediaire.
// - L. 554-3 "pourra ordonner" - court liberty to order judgment
//   insertion + 150 EUR cost ceiling built by rule PlafondCoutInsertion.
// - L. 583-1 1/2 - information and claim-assistance duties; third
//   sentence (end-of-rights help with OTHER regimes) - out of package
//   scope, no heads (recorded, not modeled).
// - L. 583-3 last para. - fund liberty to suspend where the allocataire
//   refuses checks; penal/administrative sanctions of L. 114-17 -
//   external articles, no heads.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package fr.pf.core version "0.1.0";
namespace "urn:fr:corpus:clir:pf-core";

